1129:source\asw/mp3.c **** /**
1130:source\asw/mp3.c ****  * \brief Scan the whole card from the root and store all WAV files in MP3__songList.
1131:source\asw/mp3.c ****  *
1132:source\asw/mp3.c ****  * Stores the full path of each WAV file, e.g. "\MUSIC\SONG.WAV". Entries
1133:source\asw/mp3.c ****  * starting with '.', hidden and system entries are skipped. The scan stops when
1134:source\asw/mp3.c ****  * the list is full. Subfolders are scanned down to MP3__SCAN_MAX_DEPTH levels.
1135:source\asw/mp3.c ****  *
1136:source\asw/mp3.c ****  * It is a loop with an explicit level counter instead of a recursive function
1137:source\asw/mp3.c ****  * (MISRA C:2012 Rule 17.2). The parent folder is closed while a subfolder is
1138:source\asw/mp3.c ****  * scanned and opened again afterwards, skipping what was already read (N6).
1139:source\asw/mp3.c ****  *
1140:source\asw/mp3.c ****  * \return RC_SUCCESS when every folder could be opened (also with 0 songs found),
1141:source\asw/mp3.c ****  *         RC_ERROR_OPEN when a folder could not be opened or reopened, the list may be
1142:source\asw/mp3.c ****  *         incomplete (UART line written, error flag set, N11)
